script:         gef.py (GEF — GDB Enhanced Features)
upstream:       https://github.com/hugsy/gef
homepage:       https://gef.readthedocs.io
license:        MIT
pin-kind:       release tag
release:        2024.06
asset:          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hugsy/gef/2024.06/gef.py
file-sha256:    12881b1d42fb490ca72896099daf5c128c7c7382be0779c8f8f7db3a9161ab6f  (gef.py, verbatim upstream)
vendored:       2026-06-20

PYTHON FLOOR — load-bearing pin: 2024.06 is the LAST GEF release that supports
Python 3.6–3.9 (`PYTHON_MIN_VERSION = (3, 6)`, no `match` statements). GEF
2025.01+ requires Python 3.10 and uses 3.10 `match`/`case` syntax. The fleet is
AlmaLinux 9, whose gdb embeds Python 3.9 — so current GEF fails to *parse* at
load (SyntaxError), spamming a traceback on every `gdb` start. DO NOT bump past
2024.06 while any managed host runs EL9 / gdb-with-Python-3.9. Verify a bump on
an EL9 host with:
  gdb -nx -batch -ex 'source ~/.config/gdb/gef.py' -ex 'gef help'
— it must print "GEF for linux ready ... using Python engine 3.9", NOT a Python
SyntaxError. (`gef-legacy` is NOT a fallback — it targets GDB+Python2.) pwndbg,
the other front-end, is immune: its portable build bundles a newer Python.

files:          gef.py  (single self-contained script; verbatim upstream, zero hand-edits)
note:           Leading-dot filename (.vendor) → chezmoi-ignored; provenance only, never deployed.
                gef.py deploys 0644 to ~/.config/gdb/gef.py and is sourced by the tracked
                ~/.gdbinit (chezmoi/dot_gdbinit.tmpl) so plain `gdb` loads the GEF UI.
                dev_machine only + Linux-only: both ~/.gdbinit and ~/.config/gdb are gated out
                on prod_machine and Windows in .chezmoiignore.tmpl (TARGET paths: .gdbinit,
                .config/gdb). The OTHER GDB front-end, pwndbg, is installed separately as a
                standalone `pwndbg` command — it is a mise tool now
                (`github:pwndbg/pwndbg` in config.dev.toml) and does NOT hook
                ~/.gdbinit, so the two never collide. No config.toml [vars] entry — pinned only here.
                Bump (ONLY once the fleet's gdb-Python ≥ the target GEF's floor — see PYTHON
                FLOOR above): re-download gef.py at the new tag, refresh release + asset +
                file-sha256 + vendored, then re-verify the load on an EL9 host. ~/.gdbinit
                needs no change.
